  "body": "The post-merge gate on `main` is red at `768fe23f0` (merge of PR #3039). The last green run was `44778591564` on `16d23d97` (merge of PR #2889), 16:57Z. The workflow opened no issue: the report job is skipped when the gate fails (known gap, #1611).\n\n## What fails\n\n`app suites: example_catalog`, one test, in 59 s (1 failed of 993 steps; clippy and all other suites green):\n\n```\ncontract::two_broken_cases_report_both_names_and_times\ncrates/app/tests/example_catalog/contract.rs:32\n```\n\nRun: 44780029308 · job 136449249192 · 2026-11-20 17:06–17:42Z.\n\n## What the test does\n\nThe test starts its own test executable twice, with `CAMCRAFT_TEST_CATALOG_ROOT` set to an empty scratch folder. It expects the two named case tests to fail fast, and to print `... FAILED` plus an `elapsed=` line for each case (#2857, #2960).\n\nThe step took 59 s. That length suggests the inner cases did real generation work: the environment override may not reach the inner run, or discovery falls back to the real `examples/catalog` when the scratch root holds no cases.\n\n## What landed between the green and the red\n\n- `b49d2b2f3` merge of PR #2787 (light tier in `xtask/`, new pins in `light_tests.rs`).\n- `768fe23f0` merge of PR #3039 (`PROCESS_VERSION 113` bump only).\n\nNo `crates/` change other than #2787's `xtask/` work landed in that window. The run on the later tip `ee91ac3e5` (PR #3041) is in progress; a green there does not fix the contract test, so check whether the red repeats before you close this.\n\n## Done means\n\nThe test fails fast on the scratch root on the Linux runner again, or its contract changes so it does not depend on the override; the post-merge run on the current `main` tip is green for this suite.\n",
